                "role": "assistant",
                "content": "# Solution\n\n## Part (1): EDTA Protonation Fraction\n\n**Derivation.** For the tetraprotic acid H\u2084Y, successive dissociation gives:\n\n$$[HY^{3-}] = \\frac{[H^+][Y^{4-}]}{K_{a4}},\\quad [H_2Y^{2-}] = \\frac{[H^+]^2[Y^{4-}]}{K_{a3}K_{a4}},\\quad \\dots$$\n\nSumming all species:\n\n$$[Y'] = [Y^{4-}]\\!\\left(1 + \\frac{[H^+]}{K_{a4}} + \\frac{[H^+]^2}{K_{a3}K_{a4}} + \\frac{[H^+]^3}{K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}} + \\frac{[H^+]^4}{K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}}\\right)$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\\boxed{\\alpha_Y = \\frac{[Y^{4-}]}{[Y']} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\dfrac{[H^+]}{K_{a4}} + \\dfrac{[H^+]^2}{K_{a3}K_{a4}} + \\dfrac{[H^+]^3}{K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}} + \\dfrac{[H^+]^4}{K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}}}}$$\n\n**Numerical evaluation at pH = 10.00** ($[H^+] = 10^{-10}$):\n\n| Term | Value |\n|------|-------|\n| $[H^+]/K_{a4} = 10^{0.26}$ | $1.820$ |\n| $[H^+]^2/(K_{a3}K_{a4}) = 10^{-3.58}$ | $2.63\\times10^{-4}$ |\n| Remaining terms | $<10^{-10}$ |\n\n$$\\alpha_Y = \\frac{1}{1 + 1.820 + 0.000263 + \\cdots} = \\frac{1}{2.820} = \\boxed{0.355}$$\n\n---\n\n## Part (2): Conditional Formation Constants\n\nStarting from the intrinsic constant and inserting the definitions of $\\alpha_M$ and $\\alpha_Y$:\n\n$$K_M'' = \\frac{[\\mathrm{MY}]}{[\\mathrm{M}'][Y']} = \\frac{[\\mathrm{MY}]}{[\\mathrm{M}^{2+}][Y^{4-}]}\\cdot\\frac{[\\mathrm{M}^{2+}]}{[\\mathrm{M}']}\\cdot\\frac{[Y^{4-}]}{[Y']} = K_f^M\\cdot\\frac{1}{\\alpha_M}\\cdot\\alpha_Y$$\n\n$$\\boxed{K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}'' = \\frac{K_f^{\\mathrm{Zn}}\\,\\alpha_Y}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{Zn}}} = \\frac{(3.00\\times10^{16})(0.3546)}{1.00\\times10^{5}} = 1.06\\times10^{12}}$$\n\n$$\\boxed{K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}'' = \\frac{K_f^{\\mathrm{Mg}}\\,\\alpha_Y}{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{Mg}}} = \\frac{(5.00\\times10^{8})(0.3546)}{10.0} = 1.77\\times10^{7}}$$\n\n---\n\n## Part (3): Nonlinear Equation in $y$\n\n**Mass balances:**\n\n$$C_{\\mathrm{Zn}} = [\\mathrm{Zn}'] + [\\mathrm{ZnY}], \\qquad C_{\\mathrm{Mg}} = [\\mathrm{Mg}'] + [\\mathrm{MgY}]$$\n\n$$C_Y = [Y'] + [\\mathrm{ZnY}] + [\\mathrm{MgY}]$$\n\nFrom the conditional formation constants: $[\\mathrm{MY}] = K_M''[\\mathrm{M}']y$. Substituting $[\\mathrm{M}'] = C_M - [\\mathrm{MY}]$ and solving:\n\n$$[\\mathrm{MY}] = \\frac{K_M''\\,C_M\\,y}{1 + K_M''\\,y}$$\n\nInserting both into the EDTA mass balance yields the **single nonlinear equation in $y$**:\n\n$$\\boxed{C_Y = y + \\frac{K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}''\\,C_{\\mathrm{Zn}}\\,y}{1 + K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}''\\,y} + \\frac{K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''\\,C_{\\mathrm{Mg}}\\,y}{1 + K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''\\,y}}$$\n\nwith $C_Y = 1.20\\times10^{-3}$, $C_{\\mathrm{Zn}} = C_{\\mathrm{Mg}} = 1.00\\times10^{-3}$.\n\n---\n\n## Part (4): Solution and Concentrations\n\nSince $K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}''\\,y \\gg 1$ (as will be verified), the Zn term saturates to $C_{\\mathrm{Zn}}$. The equation reduces to:\n\n$$C_Y - C_{\\mathrm{Zn}} \\approx \\frac{K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''\\,C_{\\mathrm{Mg}}\\,y}{1 + K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''\\,y}$$\n\nLetting $u = K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''\\,y$:\n\n$$0.20\\times10^{-3} = \\frac{u\\times10^{-3}}{1+u} \\implies 0.20(1+u) = u \\implies u = 0.25$$\n\n$$y = \\frac{0.25}{K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''} = \\frac{0.25}{1.773\\times10^{7}} = 1.41\\times10^{-8}\\ \\mathrm{M}$$\n\n**Verification:** $K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}''\\,y = (1.064\\times10^{12})(1.41\\times10^{-8}) = 1.50\\times10^{4}\\gg 1$ \u2713, and $y/C_Y \\approx 10^{-5}$ (negligible) \u2713.\n\n**All concentrations:**\n\n| Species | Expression | Value |\n|---------|-----------|-------|\n| $[\\mathrm{ZnY}^{2-}]$ | $\\dfrac{K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}''\\,C_{\\mathrm{Zn}}\\,y}{1+K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}''\\,y}$ | $\\mathbf{1.00\\times10^{-3}}$ |\n| $[\\mathrm{MgY}^{2-}]$ | $\\dfrac{K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''\\,C_{\\mathrm{Mg}}\\,y}{1+K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''\\,y} = \\dfrac{0.25}{1.25}\\times10^{-3}$ | $\\mathbf{2.00\\times10^{-4}}$ |\n| $[\\mathrm{Zn}']$ | $\\dfrac{C_{\\mathrm{Zn}}}{1+K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}''\\,y} = \\dfrac{10^{-3}}{1.50\\times10^{4}}$ | $\\mathbf{6.67\\times10^{-8}}$ |\n| $[\\mathrm{Mg}']$ | $\\dfrac{C_{\\mathrm{Mg}}}{1+K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''\\,y} = \\dfrac{10^{-3}}{1.25}$ | $\\mathbf{8.00\\times10^{-4}}$ |\n| $[\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}]$ | $[\\mathrm{Zn}']/\\alpha_{\\mathrm{Zn}}$ | $\\mathbf{6.67\\times10^{-13}}$ |\n| $[\\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}]$ | $[\\mathrm{Mg}']/\\alpha_{\\mathrm{Mg}}$ | $\\mathbf{8.00\\times10^{-5}}$ |\n\n**Check:** $y + [\\mathrm{ZnY}] + [\\mathrm{MgY}] = 1.41\\times10^{-8} + 9.999\\times10^{-4} + 2.00\\times10^{-4} = 1.20\\times10^{-3}$ \u2713\n\n---\n\n## Part (5): $p\\mathrm{Zn}$ and $p\\mathrm{Mg}$\n\n$$\\boxed{p\\mathrm{Zn} = -\\log_{10}(6.67\\times10^{-13}) = 12.2}$$\n\n$$\\boxed{p\\mathrm{Mg} = -\\log_{10}(8.00\\times10^{-5}) = 4.10}$$\n\n---\n\n## Part (6): Conditional Exchange Constant\n\n**Derivation.** The exchange reaction is:\n\n$$\\mathrm{Zn' + MgY \\rightleftharpoons ZnY + Mg'}$$\n\n$$K_{\\mathrm{ex}} = \\frac{[\\mathrm{ZnY}][\\mathrm{Mg}']}{[\\mathrm{Zn}'][\\mathrm{MgY}]} = \\frac{[\\mathrm{ZnY}]}{[\\mathrm{Zn}'][Y']} \\cdot \\frac{[\\mathrm{Mg}'][Y']}{[\\mathrm{MgY}]} = \\frac{K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}''}{K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}''}$$\n\n$$\\boxed{K_{\\mathrm{ex}} = \\frac{1.06\\times10^{12}}{1.77\\times10^{7}} = 6.00\\times10^{4}}$$\n\n**Verification with computed values:**\n\n$$K_{\\mathrm{ex}} = \\frac{(1.00\\times10^{-3})(8.00\\times10^{-4})}{(6.67\\times10^{-8})(2.00\\times10^{-4})} = \\frac{8.00\\times10^{-7}}{1.33\\times10^{-11}} = 6.00\\times10^{4}\\;\\checkmark$$\n\n**Why $K_{\\mathrm{ex}}$ large does not force $[\\mathrm{MgY}]=0$:**\n\nThe equilibrium condition is the *ratio*:\n\n$$\\frac{[\\mathrm{ZnY}][\\mathrm{Mg}']}{[\\mathrm{Zn}'][\\mathrm{MgY}]} = 6.00\\times10^{4}$$\n\nSolving for $[\\mathrm{MgY}]$:\n\n$$[\\mathrm{MgY}] = \\frac{[\\mathrm{ZnY}][\\mathrm{Mg}']}{K_{\\mathrm{ex}}\\,[\\mathrm{Zn}']}$$\n\nA large $K_{\\mathrm{ex}}$ drives $[\\mathrm{MgY}]$ small *relative to* $[\\mathrm{ZnY}][\\mathrm{Mg}']/[\\mathrm{Zn}]$, but $[\\mathrm{Zn}']$ itself is already extremely small ($\\sim 10^{-8}$) because Zn is almost entirely sequestered as ZnY. This small denominator partially offsets the large $K_{\\mathrm{ex}}$, leaving $[\\mathrm{MgY}] = 2.00\\times10^{-4}$ \u2014 a perfectly finite, non-negligible concentration. The equilibrium constant constrains a *ratio of four concentrations*, not the absolute value of any single one.",
                "reasoning_content": "Let me work through this problem step by step.\n\n**Part (1): EDTA protonation fraction**\n\nFor H\u2084Y with dissociation constants K_{a1}, K_{a2}, K_{a3}, K_{a4}:\n\nH\u2084Y \u21cc H\u207a + H\u2083Y\u207b, K_{a1}\nH\u2083Y\u207b \u21cc H\u207a + H\u2082Y\u00b2\u207b, K_{a2}\nH\u2082Y\u00b2\u207b \u21cc H\u207a + HY\u00b3\u207b, K_{a3}\nHY\u00b3\u207b \u21cc H\u207a + Y\u2074\u207b, K_{a4}\n\nThe total concentration of all protonation states:\n[Y'] = [H\u2084Y] + [H\u2083Y\u207b] + [H\u2082Y\u00b2\u207b] + [HY\u00b3\u207b] + [Y\u2074\u207b]\n\nWe need \u03b1_Y = [Y\u2074\u207b]/[Y']\n\nLet me express everything in terms of [Y\u2074\u207b] and [H\u207a]:\n\nFrom K_{a4}: [HY\u00b3\u207b] = [H\u207a][Y\u2074\u207b]/K_{a4}\nFrom K_{a3}: [H\u2082Y\u00b2\u207b] = [H\u207a][HY\u00b3\u207b]/K_{a3} = [H\u207a]\u00b2[Y\u2074\u207b]/(K_{a3}K_{a4})\nFrom K_{a2}: [H\u2083Y\u207b] = [H\u207a][H\u2082Y\u00b2\u207b]/K_{a2} = [H\u207a]\u00b3[Y\u2074\u207b]/(K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4})\nFrom K_{a1}: [H\u2084Y] = [H\u207a][H\u2083Y\u207b]/K_{a1} = [H\u207a]\u2074[Y\u2074\u207b]/(K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4})\n\nSo:\n[Y'] = [Y\u2074\u207b](1 + [H\u207a]/K_{a4} + [H\u207a]\u00b2/(K_{a3}K_{a4}) + [H\u207a]\u00b3/(K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}) + [H\u207a]\u2074/(K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}))\n\nTherefore:\n\u03b1_Y = [Y\u2074\u207b]/[Y'] = 1/(1 + [H\u207a]/K_{a4} + [H\u207a]\u00b2/(K_{a3}K_{a4}) + [H\u207a]\u00b3/(K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}) + [H\u207a]\u2074/(K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}))\n\nOr equivalently:\n\u03b1_Y = K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4} / ([H\u207a]\u2074 + [H\u207a]\u00b3K_{a1} + [H\u207a]\u00b2K_{a1}K_{a2} + [H\u207a]K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3} + K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4})\n\nNow let me evaluate at pH = 10.00, so [H\u207a] = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070.\n\nK_{a1} = 10\u207b\u00b2\u00b7\u2070\u2070 = 1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b2\nK_{a2} = 10\u207b\u00b2\u00b7\u2076\u2077 = 2.138 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\nK_{a3} = 10\u207b\u2076\u00b7\u00b9\u2076 = 6.918 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2077\nK_{a4} = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076 = 5.495 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b9\n\n[H\u207a] = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\n\nLet me compute each term in the denominator of \u03b1_Y (the form with 1 + ...):\n\nTerm 0: 1\nTerm 1: [H\u207a]/K_{a4} = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070 / 5.495 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b9 = 100/5.495 = 18.20\n\nWait, let me be more careful.\n\n10\u207b\u00b9\u2070 / 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076 = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u207a\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076 = 10\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076 = 1.820\n\nTerm 2: [H\u207a]\u00b2/(K_{a3}K_{a4}) = 10\u207b\u00b2\u2070/(10\u207b\u2076\u00b7\u00b9\u2076 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076) = 10\u207b\u00b2\u2070/10\u207b\u00b9\u2076\u00b7\u2074\u00b2 = 10\u207b\u00b2\u2070\u207a\u00b9\u2076\u00b7\u2074\u00b2 = 10\u207b\u00b3\u00b7\u2075\u2078 = 2.63 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\nTerm 3: [H\u207a]\u00b3/(K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}) = 10\u207b\u00b3\u2070/(10\u207b\u00b2\u00b7\u2076\u2077 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2076\u00b7\u00b9\u2076 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076) = 10\u207b\u00b3\u2070/10\u207b\u00b9\u2079\u00b7\u2070\u2079 = 10\u207b\u00b3\u2070\u207a\u00b9\u2079\u00b7\u2070\u2079 = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u2079\u00b9 \u2248 1.23 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b9\n\nTerm 4: [H\u207a]\u2074/(K_{a1}K_{a2}K_{a3}K_{a4}) = 10\u207b\u2074\u2070/(10\u207b\u00b2\u00b7\u2070\u2070 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b2\u00b7\u2076\u2077 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2076\u00b7\u00b9\u2076 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076) = 10\u207b\u2074\u2070/10\u207b\u00b2\u00b9\u00b7\u2070\u2079 = 10\u207b\u2074\u2070\u207a\u00b2\u00b9\u00b7\u2070\u2079 = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2078\u00b7\u2079\u00b9 \u2248 1.23 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2079\n\nSo \u03b1_Y = 1/(1 + 1.820 + 2.63 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 + ...) \u2248 1/(2.820) \u2248 0.3546\n\nLet me be more precise:\n10\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076 = 10^0.26\n\nlog\u2081\u2080(1.82) = 0.2602... so 10^0.26 \u2248 1.8197\n\nSo \u03b1_Y = 1/(1 + 1.8197 + 0.000263 + ...) \u2248 1/2.8200 \u2248 0.3546\n\nLet me compute more precisely:\n1 + 1.8197 + 0.000263 + ... = 2.81996...\n\n\u03b1_Y = 1/2.81996 = 0.35461...\n\nSo \u03b1_Y \u2248 0.355 (to 3 sig figs).\n\nWait, let me double-check: 1/2.82 = 0.35461...\n\nYes, \u03b1_Y \u2248 0.355.\n\n**Part (2): Conditional formation constants**\n\nThe conditional formation constant is defined as:\nK_M'' = [MY]/([M'][Y'])\n\nWe know:\nK_f^M = [MY]/([M\u00b2\u207a][Y\u2074\u207b])\n\nSo:\nK_M'' = [MY]/([M'][Y']) = [MY]/([M\u00b2\u207a][Y\u2074\u207b]) \u00d7 [M\u00b2\u207a]/[M'] \u00d7 [Y\u2074\u207b]/[Y']\n\n= K_f^M \u00d7 (1/\u03b1_M) \u00d7 \u03b1_Y\n\nTherefore:\nK_Zn'' = K_f^Zn \u00d7 \u03b1_Y / \u03b1_Zn\nK_Mg'' = K_f^Mg \u00d7 \u03b1_Y / \u03b1_Mg\n\nK_Zn'' = (3.00 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u2076) \u00d7 0.3546 / (1.00 \u00d7 10\u2075) = 3.00 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u2076 \u00d7 0.3546 / 10\u2075 = 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2\n\nWait, let me recalculate with the more precise value of \u03b1_Y.\n\n\u03b1_Y = 1/(1 + 10^0.26 + 10^-3.58 + ...)\n\n10^0.26: Let me compute this more carefully.\n0.26 \u00d7 ln(10) = 0.26 \u00d7 2.3026 = 0.5987\ne^0.5987 = 1.8197\n\n10^-3.58: \n-3.58 \u00d7 ln(10) = -8.2433\ne^-8.2433 \u2248 2.63 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\nSo denominator = 1 + 1.8197 + 0.000263 \u2248 2.81996\n\n\u03b1_Y = 1/2.81996 = 0.35461\n\nK_Zn'' = (3.00 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u2076)(0.35461)/(1.00 \u00d7 10\u2075) = (1.0638 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u2076)/(10\u2075) = 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2\n\nK_Mg'' = (5.00 \u00d7 10\u2078)(0.35461)/(10.0) = (1.773 \u00d7 10\u2078)/(10) = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077\n\nLet me be more precise:\nK_Zn'' = 3.00 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u2076 \u00d7 0.35461 / 10\u2075 = 1.06383 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2\nK_Mg'' = 5.00 \u00d7 10\u2078 \u00d7 0.35461 / 10 = 1.77305 \u00d7 10\u2077\n\nSo K_Zn'' \u2248 1.06 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 and K_Mg'' \u2248 1.77 \u00d7 10\u2077.\n\n**Part (3): Mass balance equation in y**\n\nLet y = [Y']\n\nMass balance for EDTA:\nC_Y = [Y'] + [ZnY] + [MgY]\n1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = y + [ZnY] + [MgY] ... (i)\n\nMass balance for Zn:\nC_Zn = [Zn'] + [ZnY]\n1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = [Zn'] + [ZnY] ... (ii)\n\nMass balance for Mg:\nC_Mg = [Mg'] + [MgY]\n1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = [Mg'] + [MgY] ... (iii)\n\nFrom the conditional formation constants:\n[ZnY] = K_Zn'' \u00d7 [Zn'] \u00d7 [Y'] = K_Zn'' \u00d7 [Zn'] \u00d7 y\n[MgY] = K_Mg'' \u00d7 [Mg'] \u00d7 [Y'] = K_Mg'' \u00d7 [Mg'] \u00d7 y\n\nFrom (ii): [Zn'] = C_Zn - [ZnY]\nFrom (iii): [Mg'] = C_Mg - [MgY]\n\nSubstituting:\n[ZnY] = K_Zn'' \u00d7 (C_Zn - [ZnY]) \u00d7 y\n[ZnY] = K_Zn'' \u00d7 y \u00d7 C_Zn - K_Zn'' \u00d7 y \u00d7 [ZnY]\n[ZnY](1 + K_Zn'' \u00d7 y) = K_Zn'' \u00d7 y \u00d7 C_Zn\n[ZnY] = K_Zn'' \u00d7 y \u00d7 C_Zn / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00d7 y)\n\nSimilarly:\n[MgY] = K_Mg'' \u00d7 y \u00d7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00d7 y)\n\nNow substitute into (i):\nC_Y = y + K_Zn'' \u00d7 y \u00d7 C_Zn / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00d7 y) + K_Mg'' \u00d7 y \u00d7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00d7 y)\n\nThis is the nonlinear equation in y.\n\nLet me write it more cleanly:\nC_Y = y + \\frac{K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}'' \\cdot y \\cdot C_{\\mathrm{Zn}}}{1 + K_{\\mathrm{Zn}}'' \\cdot y} + \\frac{K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}'' \\cdot y \\cdot C_{\\mathrm{Mg}}}{1 + K_{\\mathrm{Mg}}'' \\cdot y}\n\n**Part (4): Solve for y**\n\nLet me plug in numbers:\nC_Y = 1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\nC_Zn = 1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\nC_Mg = 1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\nK_Zn'' = 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2\nK_Mg'' = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077\n\nThe equation is:\n1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = y + (1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2)(y)(10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u00b7 y) + (1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077)(y)(10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00b7 y)\n\nLet me simplify the fractions:\nFirst term: (1.064 \u00d7 10\u2079 \u00b7 y)/(1 + 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u00b7 y)\nSecond term: (1.773 \u00d7 10\u2074 \u00b7 y)/(1 + 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00b7 y)\n\nSince K_Zn'' is very large, the first fraction will be approximately C_Zn = 10\u207b\u00b3 (as long as K_Zn'' \u00b7 y >> 1, i.e., y >> 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b2).\n\nFor K_Mg'' = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077, we need K_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00b7 y. If y is around 10\u207b\u2075, then K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u2248 177, which is >> 1. If y is around 10\u207b\u2077, then K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u2248 1.77, which is not >> 1.\n\nLet me think about what y should be. If Zn captures almost all of its EDTA (\u2248 10\u207b\u00b3) and Mg captures some, then:\nC_Y = y + [ZnY] + [MgY]\n1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u2248 y + 1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 + [MgY]\n\nSo y + [MgY] \u2248 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 2.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\nIf K_Mg'' \u00b7 y >> 1, then [MgY] \u2248 C_Mg = 10\u207b\u00b3, which would give y + 10\u207b\u00b3 \u2248 2 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074, which is impossible (y would be negative).\n\nSo K_Mg'' \u00b7 y must be of order 1 or less. Let's try K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u2248 1, so y \u2248 1/(1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077) \u2248 5.6 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078.\n\nLet me try y = 5.6 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 5.6 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.993 \u2248 1\n\n[MgY] = (1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 5.6 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.993) = (0.993 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1.993) = 0.498 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\n[ZnY] \u2248 10\u207b\u00b3 (since K_Zn'' \u00b7 y = 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u00d7 5.6 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 5.96 \u00d7 10\u2074 >> 1)\n\nCheck: y + [ZnY] + [MgY] = 5.6 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.498 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.498 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nBut we need 1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3. So y is too large (or [MgY] is too large). We need [MgY] to be smaller, which means y should be smaller.\n\nLet me try y = 3.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 3.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.532\n[MgY] = (0.532 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.532) = 0.532/1.532 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.347 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\n[ZnY] \u2248 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: y + [ZnY] + [MgY] = 3.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.347 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.347 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nStill too large. Need smaller y.\n\nLet me try y = 1.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 1.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.1773\n[MgY] = (0.1773 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.1773) = 0.1773/1.1773 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.1506 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\n[ZnY] \u2248 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 1.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.1506 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.1506 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nStill a bit too large. Need slightly smaller y.\n\nLet me try y = 0.5 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 5 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 5 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079 = 0.08865\n[MgY] = (0.08865 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.08865) = 0.08865/1.08865 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.08143 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 5 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.08143 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.0814 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nToo small now. Need y between 5 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079 and 1.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078.\n\nLet me try y = 7.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 7.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079 = 0.12411\n[MgY] = (0.12411 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.12411) = 0.12411/1.12411 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.11041 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 7.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.11041 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.1104 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nStill too small.\n\nLet me try y = 9.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 9.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079 = 0.15957\n[MgY] = (0.15957 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.15957) = 0.15957/1.15957 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.13762 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 9.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2079 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.13762 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.1376 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nStill too small.\n\nLet me try y = 1.5 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 1.5 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.26595\n[MgY] = (0.26595 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.26595) = 0.26595/1.26595 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.20999 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 1.5 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.20999 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.2100 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nThat's very close to 1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3! Let me try y = 1.45 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 1.45 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.25709\n[MgY] = (0.25709 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.25709) = 0.25709/1.25709 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.20452 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 1.45 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.20452 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.2045 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nStill slightly too large.\n\nLet me try y = 1.40 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 1.40 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.24822\n[MgY] = (0.24822 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.24822) = 0.24822/1.24822 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.19886 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 1.40 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.19886 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.1989 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nVery close! Let me try y = 1.42 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 1.42 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.25177\n[MgY] = (0.25177 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1 + 0.25177) = 0.25177/1.25177 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.20113 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 1.42 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.20113 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.2011 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nClose. Let me try y = 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.25000 (approximately)\n\nLet me compute: 1.773 \u00d7 1.41 = 2.49993, so K_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 0.24999\n\n[MgY] = (0.24999 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)/(1.24999) = 0.20000 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nCheck: 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.20000 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.2000 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nThat's essentially exact! So y \u2248 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078.\n\nActually, let me be more careful. Let me solve this more precisely.\n\nThe equation is:\nC_Y = y + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Zn / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y) + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y)\n\nSince K_Zn'' \u00b7 y = 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u00d7 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 \u2248 1.5 \u00d7 10\u2074 >> 1, the first term is essentially C_Zn = 10\u207b\u00b3.\n\nMore precisely: K_Zn'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Zn / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y) = C_Zn \u00b7 K_Zn'' \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y) = C_Zn / (1 + 1/(K_Zn'' \u00b7 y))\n\n= 10\u207b\u00b3 / (1 + 1/(1.5 \u00d7 10\u2074)) \u2248 10\u207b\u00b3(1 - 6.7 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2075) \u2248 10\u207b\u00b3 - 6.7 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n\nThis correction is negligible compared to y itself.\n\nSo the equation reduces to:\nC_Y \u2248 C_Zn + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) + y\n\n1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u2248 1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) + y\n\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u2248 K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) + y\n\nSince y << 2 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074, we can neglect y on the right:\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u2248 K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y)\n\nLet me define u = K_Mg'' \u00b7 y:\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = u \u00b7 10\u207b\u00b3 / (1 + u)\n0.20(1 + u) = u\n0.20 + 0.20u = u\n0.20 = 0.80u\nu = 0.25\n\nSo K_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 0.25\ny = 0.25 / K_Mg'' = 0.25 / (1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077) = 1.410 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n\nNow let me include the small correction from y and from the Zn term:\n\nC_Y - C_Zn = K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) + y\n\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.25 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 / (1.25) + y\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 + y\n\nWait, that gives y = 0. That can't be right. Let me redo.\n\nActually, I made an error. Let me be more careful.\n\nK_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) with K_Mg'' \u00b7 y = 0.25:\n= 0.25 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 / 1.25 = 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nSo: C_Y = C_Zn + 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 + y\n1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 + y\n1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 + y\n\nThis gives y = 0, which means the correction from y is of order y itself, and we need to be more careful.\n\nActually, this makes sense. The equation is:\nC_Y = C_Zn + [MgY] + y (to good approximation, since [ZnY] \u2248 C_Zn)\n\nAnd [MgY] = K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y)\n\nSo: C_Y - C_Zn = K_Mg'' \u00b7 y \u00b7 C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) + y\n\nLet f(y) = K_Mg'' \u00b7 C_Mg \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) + y\n\nWe need f(y) = C_Y - C_Zn = 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nLet me solve this more carefully. Let a = K_Mg'' = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 and b = C_Mg = 10\u207b\u00b3.\n\nf(y) = a\u00b7b\u00b7y/(1+a\u00b7y) + y = y(1 + a\u00b7b/(1+a\u00b7y)) = y((1+a\u00b7y + a\u00b7b)/(1+a\u00b7y)) = y(1 + a\u00b7y + a\u00b7b)/(1 + a\u00b7y)\n\nWe need: y(1 + a\u00b7y + a\u00b7b)/(1 + a\u00b7y) = 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nLet me try y = 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078:\na\u00b7y = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 0.24999\n1 + a\u00b7y = 1.24999\na\u00b7b = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2074\n1 + a\u00b7y + a\u00b7b = 1.24999 + 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2074 \u2248 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2074\n\nf(y) = 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 \u00d7 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2074 / 1.24999 = 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 \u00d7 1.4185 \u00d7 10\u2074 = 1.9999 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\nHmm, that's 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3. So y = 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 is very close.\n\nActually, let me just solve the quadratic more directly.\n\ny(1 + a\u00b7y + a\u00b7b) = (0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3)(1 + a\u00b7y)\ny + a\u00b7y\u00b2 + a\u00b7b\u00b7y = 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 + 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00b7 a\u00b7y\na\u00b7y\u00b2 + y(1 + a\u00b7b - 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00b7 a) = 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nSince a\u00b7b = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2074 >> 1 and 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00b7 a = 3546, we have:\n1 + a\u00b7b - 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00b7 a \u2248 a\u00b7b = 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2074\n\nSo: a\u00b7y\u00b2 + a\u00b7b\u00b7y \u2248 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\na\u00b7y(y + b) \u2248 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nSince y << b (y ~ 10\u207b\u2078, b = 10\u207b\u00b3):\na\u00b7b\u00b7y \u2248 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\ny \u2248 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 / (a\u00b7b) = 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 / (1.773 \u00d7 10\u2074) = 1.128 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n\nHmm, that's different from what I got before. Let me recheck.\n\nWait, I think I made an error. Let me redo.\n\nThe equation is:\nC_Y = y + [ZnY] + [MgY]\n\nWhere:\n[ZnY] = K_Zn'' \u00b7 [Zn'] \u00b7 y\n[MgY] = K_Mg'' \u00b7 [Mg'] \u00b7 y\n\nAnd:\n[Zn'] = C_Zn - [ZnY]\n[Mg'] = C_Mg - [MgY]\n\nSo:\n[ZnY] = K_Zn'' \u00b7 (C_Zn - [ZnY]) \u00b7 y\n[ZnY](1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y) = K_Zn'' \u00b7 C_Zn \u00b7 y\n[ZnY] = K_Zn'' \u00b7 C_Zn \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y)\n\nSimilarly:\n[MgY] = K_Mg'' \u00b7 C_Mg \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y)\n\nThe EDTA mass balance:\nC_Y = y + K_Zn'' \u00b7 C_Zn \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y) + K_Mg'' \u00b7 C_Mg \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y)\n\nNow, for K_Zn'' \u00b7 y >> 1:\nK_Zn'' \u00b7 C_Zn \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y) \u2248 C_Zn(1 - 1/(K_Zn'' \u00b7 y)) \u2248 C_Zn\n\nSo: C_Y \u2248 y + C_Zn + K_Mg'' \u00b7 C_Mg \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y)\n\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u2248 y + K_Mg'' \u00b7 C_Mg \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y)\n\nSince y ~ 10\u207b\u2078 and 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 2 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074, y is negligible compared to the other term. So:\n\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u2248 K_Mg'' \u00b7 C_Mg \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y)\n\nLet u = K_Mg'' \u00b7 y:\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = u \u00b7 10\u207b\u00b3 / (1 + u)\n0.20(1 + u) = u\n0.20 + 0.20u = u\n0.20 = 0.80u\nu = 0.25\n\ny = 0.25 / K_Mg'' = 0.25 / (1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077)\n\nLet me compute: 0.25 / 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 = 0.1410 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2077 = 1.410 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n\nNow let me check if y is indeed negligible:\ny = 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 vs 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 2 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\ny/(0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3) = 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 / 2 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 = 7.05 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2075\n\nSo y is about 0.007% of the target, which is negligible. Good.\n\nSo y \u2248 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 M.\n\nNow let me compute all the concentrations:\n\n[ZnY] = K_Zn'' \u00b7 C_Zn \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y)\nK_Zn'' \u00b7 y = 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u00d7 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 1.500 \u00d7 10\u2074\n[ZnY] = 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00d7 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 / (1 + 1.500 \u00d7 10\u2074)\n= 1.500 \u00d7 10\u2074 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 / (1.500 \u00d7 10\u2074 + 1)\n= 15.00 / 15001 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\u2248 0.99993 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\u2248 1.000 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\nMore precisely: [ZnY] = C_Zn \u00d7 K_Zn'' \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y) = 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00d7 15000/15001 = 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00d7 (1 - 1/15001) \u2248 10\u207b\u00b3(1 - 6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2075)\n\n[ZnY] \u2248 9.999 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 \u2248 1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 (to 3 sig figs)\n\n[MgY] = K_Mg'' \u00b7 C_Mg \u00b7 y / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) = 0.25 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 / 1.25 = 0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = 2.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\n[Zn'] = C_Zn - [ZnY] = 10\u207b\u00b3 - 9.999 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 = 6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n\nActually, let me be more precise:\n[Zn'] = C_Zn / (1 + K_Zn'' \u00b7 y) = 10\u207b\u00b3 / (1 + 15000) = 10\u207b\u00b3 / 15001 = 6.666 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n\n[Mg'] = C_Mg / (1 + K_Mg'' \u00b7 y) = 10\u207b\u00b3 / (1 + 0.25) = 10\u207b\u00b3 / 1.25 = 8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\n[Zn\u00b2\u207a] = [Zn'] / \u03b1_Zn = 6.666 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 / 10\u2075 = 6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b3\n\n[Mg\u00b2\u207a] = [Mg'] / \u03b1_Mg = 8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 / 10 = 8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2075\n\nLet me verify the EDTA mass balance:\ny + [ZnY] + [MgY] = 1.41 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 + 9.999 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 + 2.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 = 1.200 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 \u2713\n\n**Part (5): pZn and pMg**\n\npZn = -log\u2081\u2080(6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b3) = 13 - log\u2081\u2080(6.67) = 13 - 0.824 = 12.176 \u2248 12.2\n\npMg = -log\u2081\u2080(8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2075) = 5 - log\u2081\u2080(8.00) = 5 - 0.903 = 4.097 \u2248 4.10\n\n**Part (6): Exchange reaction**\n\nZn' + MgY \u21cc ZnY + Mg'\n\nK_exchange = [ZnY][Mg'] / ([Zn'][MgY])\n\nNow, from the conditional formation constants:\nK_Zn'' = [ZnY]/([Zn'][Y'])\nK_Mg'' = [MgY]/([Mg'][Y'])\n\nSo: K_Zn''/K_Mg'' = ([ZnY]/([Zn'][Y'])) / ([MgY]/([Mg'][Y'])) = [ZnY][Mg'] / ([Zn'][MgY])\n\nTherefore: K_exchange = K_Zn''/K_Mg'' = 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 / 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 = 6.00 \u00d7 10\u2074\n\nLet me compute: 1.064 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 / 1.773 \u00d7 10\u2077 = (1.064/1.773) \u00d7 10\u2075 = 0.6001 \u00d7 10\u2075 = 6.00 \u00d7 10\u2074\n\nNow, why doesn't a very large K_exchange imply MgY = 0?\n\nThe exchange equilibrium is:\nK_exchange = [ZnY][Mg'] / ([Zn'][MgY])\n\nThis means: [MgY] = [ZnY][Mg'] / (K_exchange \u00d7 [Zn'])\n\nEven though K_exchange is large (6 \u00d7 10\u2074), the ratio [Zn'] / [Mg'] can be very small, which keeps [MgY] finite. In our case:\n\n[MgY] = [ZnY][Mg'] / (K_exchange \u00d7 [Zn']) = (10\u207b\u00b3)(8 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074) / (6 \u00d7 10\u2074 \u00d7 6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078)\n\n= 8 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2077 / (4.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3) = 2.0 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\nThe key point is that the equilibrium constant tells us about the ratio of products to reactants, not about absolute concentrations. Even with a large K, if the reactant [Zn'] is very small (which it is, because Zn is almost completely complexed), then the product [MgY] need not be zero. The equilibrium is determined by all four species, not just K.\n\nMore fundamentally: K_exchange = 6 \u00d7 10\u2074 means that at equilibrium, [ZnY][Mg'] = 6 \u00d7 10\u2074 \u00d7 [Zn'][MgY]. This doesn't require [MgY] = 0; it only requires the ratio [ZnY][Mg']/([Zn'][MgY]) = 6 \u00d7 10\u2074. Since [Zn'] is extremely small (~10\u207b\u2078), even a non-negligible [MgY] (~10\u207b\u2074) is consistent with equilibrium.\n\nLet me now write up a clean solution.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the precision of my calculations.\n\n\u03b1_Y at pH = 10:\n[H\u207a] = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\nK_{a1} = 10\u207b\u00b2 = 0.01\nK_{a2} = 10\u207b\u00b2\u00b7\u2076\u2077\nK_{a3} = 10\u207b\u2076\u00b7\u00b9\u2076\nK_{a4} = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076\n\n10\u207b\u00b2\u00b7\u2076\u2077: \n-2.67 \u00d7 ln(10) = -6.148\ne^(-6.148) = 0.002138\nSo K_{a2} = 2.138 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\n10\u207b\u2076\u00b7\u00b9\u2076:\n-6.16 \u00d7 ln(10) = -14.184\ne^(-14.184) = 6.918 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2077\nSo K_{a3} = 6.918 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2077\n\n10\u207b\u00b9\u2070\u00b7\u00b2\u2076:\n-10.26 \u00d7 ln(10) = -23.625\ne^(-23.625) = 5.495 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b9\nSo K_{a4} = 5.495 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b9\n\nNow:\n[H\u207a]/K_{a4} = 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070 / 5.495 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b9 = 1.820 (this is 10^0.26)\n\n10^0.26:\n0.26 \u00d7 ln(10) = 0.5987\ne^0.5987 = 1.8197\n\n[H\u207a]\u00b2/(K_{a3}K_{a4}) = 10\u207b\u00b2\u2070/(6.918 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2077 \u00d7 5.495 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b9) = 10\u207b\u00b2\u2070/(3.801 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2077) = 2.631 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\nThe other terms are negligible.\n\nSo \u03b1_Y = 1/(1 + 1.8197 + 0.0002631) = 1/2.8200 = 0.35461\n\nK_Zn'' = 3.00 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u2076 \u00d7 0.35461 / 10\u2075 = 1.0638 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2\n\nK_Mg'' = 5.00 \u00d7 10\u2078 \u00d7 0.35461 / 10 = 1.7731 \u00d7 10\u2077\n\nNow for y:\nu = K_Mg'' \u00b7 y\n0.20 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3 = u \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3/(1+u)\n0.20(1+u) = u\n0.20 = 0.80u\nu = 0.25\n\ny = 0.25/(1.7731 \u00d7 10\u2077) = 1.4100 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n\n[ZnY] = C_Zn \u00d7 K_Zn''y/(1+K_Zn''y)\nK_Zn''y = 1.0638 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u00d7 1.4100 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078 = 1.4999 \u00d7 10\u2074 \u2248 1.500 \u00d7 10\u2074\n[ZnY] = 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00d7 15000/15001 = 9.9993 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\nTo 3 sig figs: [ZnY] = 1.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\n\n[MgY] = C_Mg \u00d7 K_Mg''y/(1+K_Mg''y) = 10\u207b\u00b3 \u00d7 0.25/1.25 = 2.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\n[Zn'] = C_Zn - [ZnY] = 10\u207b\u00b3 - 9.9993 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 = 6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\nOr: [Zn'] = C_Zn/(1+K_Zn''y) = 10\u207b\u00b3/15001 = 6.666 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n\n[Mg'] = C_Mg/(1+K_Mg''y) = 10\u207b\u00b3/1.25 = 8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\n[Zn\u00b2\u207a] = [Zn']/\u03b1_Zn = 6.666 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078/10\u2075 = 6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b3\n\n[Mg\u00b2\u207a] = [Mg']/\u03b1_Mg = 8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074/10 = 8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2075\n\npZn = -log(6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b3) = 12.176 \u2248 12.2\npMg = -log(8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2075) = 4.097 \u2248 4.10\n\nK_exchange = K_Zn''/K_Mg'' = 1.0638 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2/1.7731 \u00d7 10\u2077 = 6.000 \u00d7 10\u2074\n\nLet me verify: 1.0638/1.7731 = 0.6000. Yes.\n\nSo K_exchange = 6.00 \u00d7 10\u2074.\n\nLet me double-check the exchange constant interpretation:\nK_exchange = [ZnY][Mg']/([Zn'][MgY])\n\nAt equilibrium:\n[ZnY] = 9.999 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074 \u2248 10\u207b\u00b3\n[Mg'] = 8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n[Zn'] = 6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078\n[MgY] = 2.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074\n\nK_exchange = (10\u207b\u00b3)(8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074)/((6.67 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2078)(2.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2074))\n= 8.00 \u00d7 10\u207b\u2077/(1.333 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b9)\n= 6.00 \u00d7 10\u2074 \u2713\n\nGreat, everything checks out.\n\nNow let me write the final answer clearly.\n"
